.TH COLIMA-STATUS 1 "2026-07-21" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
colima-status \- bin/colima\-status — Authoritative Colima + Docker status interface for zdots.
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBcolima-status --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
bin/colima-status — Authoritative Colima + Docker status interface for zdots.

STOP — do not call `colima status` or search for the docker socket yourself.
Use this command. Colima's own runtime hardcodes homedir config (~/.colima)
whenever that directory exists and silently ignores XDG_CONFIG_HOME — this is
colima upstream behavior, not a zdots bug, and not worth fighting (decided
2026-07-04, see Z-195/Z-181). zdots treats ~/.colima as canonical and does
not probe XDG_CONFIG_HOME/colima at all.

Commands:
  socket           Print the live docker socket path; exit 1 if not present
  health           Exit 0 = running + socket present; exit 1 otherwise
  status           Human-readable status (default)
  logs             Tail the colima autostart log

Flags:
  --json           Machine-readable JSON (with any command or alone)
  --profile <p>    Colima profile name (default: $COLIMA_PROFILE or "default")
  -h, --help       Show this help

Agent pattern:
  colima-status --json            single authoritative JSON blob
  DOCKER_HOST=$(colima-status socket) docker ps
  colima-status health && docker ps
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
